{
  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "The current best (config_019: pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile; acc=0.639) has established that multiprofile > singleprofile, avgpool > transformer, and weighted > concat. However, the RNA encoder has only been tested as PCA (linear) across all multimodal runs. The image encoder comparison (resnet50 vs ViT-L) showed near-equivalence (~0.635 vs 0.639), so further image encoder exploration has low expected information gain. The RNA encoder is the largest unexplored design axis: a learned non-linear representation (scvi_n200) could capture cell-state structure that PCA misses, potentially yielding a larger gain than the marginal differences seen in image/aggregation/fusion choices. Config_031 changes only the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 while holding all other parameters at their best-known values (multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, weighted), making it the most controlled and informative next experiment. A clear improvement would confirm RNA representation quality as a key lever; a null result would indicate PCA is sufficient and redirect budget toward other axes."
}

